ering PEAK Matrix  Assessment 2026. About Position: We are looking for an experienced Data Analyst having strong knowledge on MS SQL, Healthcare Data Modeling &amp; Integration, Statistics. You will help us build scalable, efficient cloud infrastructure. You?ll implement monitoring for automated system health checks. You?ll build our CI pipeline, and train and guide the team. Role: Data Analyst-HealthcareLocation: All Persistent LocationExperience: 6 to 10 YearsJob Type: Full-Time Employment What You&#39;ll Do: Healthcare Data Analysis &amp; ReportingAnalyze large?scale US healthcare datasets including claims, eligibility, provider, utilization, and quality dataWrite and optimize complex SQL queries to extract, validate, and analyze healthcare data from relational databasesPerform data validation, reconciliation, and transformation to support accurate reporting for business and regulatory needsHealthcare Data Modeling &amp; IntegrationWork with Snowflake, MySQL, and related platforms to support healthcare data models, marts, and analytics layersCollaborate with data engineering teams to ensure reliable ingestion and integration of data from source systems (e.g., claims processing, provider systems, eligibility feeds)Support analytics initiatives related to value?based care, population health, quality improvement, and operational efficiencyProcess Mapping &amp; DocumentationCreate process flows, data lineage diagrams, and system architecture visuals using Microsoft Visio or draw.io for healthcare data workflowsDocument healthcare business rules, data definitions, metrics logic, and reporting methodologiesSupport standardization of metrics aligned with healthcare programs and reporting frameworksStakeholder Collaboration &amp; CommunicationPartner with business stakeholders including Healthcare Operations, Finance, Clinical, Quality, and Compliance teams to understand reporting needsTranslate complex healthcare data into clear, actionable insights for technical and no